{"question_id": "A-01", "arm": "maplestats_hosted", "requested_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "model_ids": ["claude-sonnet-5-5"], "tools_available": ["mcp__maplestats__call_tool", "mcp__maplestats__plan_query", "mcp__maplestats__search_tools"], "started_at": "2026-11-10T03:27:10+00:00", "duration_s": 18.7, "tool_calls": ["mcp__maplestats__search_tools", "mcp__maplestats__search_tools", "mcp__maplestats__wds_search_cubes", "mcp__maplestats__call_tool", "mcp__maplestats__search_tools", "mcp__maplestats__search_tools", "mcp__maplestats__call_tool"], "is_error": false, "response": "In 2024, 12.8% of Alberta children under 18 were living in poverty. This uses the Market Basket Measure (2023 base), which is Canada's official poverty line. The data quality rating is \"good\".\n\nUnder the after-tax Low Income Measure, a relative measure, the 2024 rate was 13.9%.\n\n| Year | MBM (2023 base) | LIM-AT |\n|---|---|---|\n| 2022 | 12.0% | 12.2% |\n| 2023 | 11.9% | 13.5% |\n| 2024 | 12.8% | 13.9% |\n\n2024 is the latest year published. The figures come from the Canadian Income Survey, released 2026-04-29.\n\nSource: Statistics Canada, Table 11-10-0135-01. The vectors are v1792632015 (MBM) and v96520326 (LIM-AT).\n\n```json\n{\"values\": [\n{\"name\": \"Alberta child poverty rate (persons under 18), Market Basket Measure 2023 base\", \"value\": 12.8, \"unit\": \"%\", \"period\": \"2024\"},\n{\"name\": \"Alberta persons under 18 in low income, LIM-after tax\", \"value\": 13.9, \"unit\": \"%\", \"period\": \"2024\"},\n{\"name\": \"Alberta child poverty rate, MBM 2023 base\", \"value\": 11.9, \"unit\": \"%\", \"period\": \"2023\"},\n{\"name\": \"Alberta child poverty rate, MBM 2023 base\", \"value\": 12.0, \"unit\": \"%\", \"period\": \"2022\"}\n],\n\"sources\": [{\"publisher\": \"Statistics Canada\", \"id\": \"Table 11-10-0135-01; vectors v1792632015, v96520326\"}],\n\"not_published\": false,\n\"abstain\": false,\n\"abstain_reason\": \"\"}\n```", "repeat": 0, "cost_usd": 0.0699849, "input_tokens": 14, "output_tokens": 1343, "cache_read_tokens": 49469, "cache_creation_tokens": 12895}
{"question_id": "A-02", "arm": "maplestats_hosted", "requested_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "model_ids": ["claude-sonnet-5-5"], "tools_available": ["mcp__maplestats__call_tool", "mcp__maplestats__plan_query", "mcp__maplestats__search_tools"], "started_at": "2026-11-10T03:27:29+00:00", "duration_s": 22.8, "tool_calls": ["mcp__maplestats__search_tools", "mcp__maplestats__search_tools", "mcp__maplestats__search_tools", "mcp__maplestats__call_tool", "mcp__maplestats__call_tool", "mcp__maplestats__call_tool", "mcp__maplestats__call_tool", "mcp__maplestats__call_tool", "mcp__maplestats__call_tool", "mcp__maplestats__search_tools", "mcp__maplestats__call_tool"], "is_error": false, "response": "Average weekly earnings for all employees in Alberta's provincial and territorial public administration (NAICS 912) were **$1,883.03 in August 2026**, the latest month published. That figure is preliminary, includes overtime, is before source deductions, and is not seasonally adjusted. StatCan rates its data quality as excellent.\n\nThe two months before were similar:\n- June 2026: $1,877.87\n- July 2026: $1,877.58\n\nStatistics Canada does not publish an hourly average for the whole industry. The hourly-wage table covers only workers paid by the hour, so I used weekly earnings instead.\n\nThe category is provincial and territorial public administration. In Alberta it is effectively the provincial government.\n\nSource: Statistics Canada, Survey of Employment, Payrolls and Hours (SEPH), Table 14-10-0203-01, vector v1560358, released 2026-10-29.\n\n```json\n{\"values\":[{\"name\":\"Average weekly earnings, all employees incl. overtime, Alberta provincial and territorial public administration (NAICS 912), unadjusted\",\"value\":1883.03,\"unit\":\"current dollars per week\",\"period\":\"2026-08\"},{\"name\":\"Same series\",\"value\":1877.58,\"unit\":\"current dollars per week\",\"period\":\"2026-07\"},{\"name\":\"Same series\",\"value\":1877.87,\"unit\":\"current dollars per week\",\"period\":\"2026-06\"}],\"sources\":[{\"publisher\":\"Statistics Canada\",\"id\":\"14-10-0203-01 / v1560358\"}],\"not_published\":false,\"abstain\":false,\"abstain_reason\":\"\"}\n```", "repeat": 0, "cost_usd": 0.0911994, "input_tokens": 20, "output_tokens": 2037, "cache_read_tokens": 99454, "cache_creation_tokens": 15211}
